                        <div class="box-blue" style="padding: 30px;">
                            <p style="font-size:1.2em;">✅ Translators bridge the gap.</p>
                            <p class="small-text">Compilers, interpreters, and assemblers turn code into machine code.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 4. CONCEPT LOOP: HLL vs LLL -->
            <section>
                <section>
                    <h2>High-Level Languages (HLL)</h2>
                    <div class="box-blue fragment" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
                        <p style="margin:0;"><strong>High-level languages</strong> are designed to be easy for humans to read and write.</p>
                        <p class="small-text" style="margin:0.4rem 0 0;">They are often <strong>portable</strong> (can run on many different computers).</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cols fragment">
                        <div class="box box-blue">
                            <strong>Examples</strong>
                            <ul class="small-text">
                                <li>Python</li>
                                <li>Java</li>
                                <li>C++</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="box">
                            <strong>Code Example</strong>
                            <pre><code class="python">Sum = Num1 + Num2</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div style="margin-top: 20px; text-align: center;">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-down blue"></i> <span class="small-text blue">Deep Dive: Low-Level
                            Languages</span>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- VERTICAL: Low-Level Languages -->
                <section data-background="#f4f6f8">
                    <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group"></i> Deep Dive: Low-Level Languages</h3>
                    <p class="small-text">Languages closer to the hardware. Hard for humans, fast for machines.</p>
                    <div class="cols">
                        <div class="box fragment">
                            <h4>1. Machine Code</h4>
                            <p class="small-text">Binary instructions (1s and 0s) executed directly by the CPU.</p>
                            <pre><code class="plaintext">1010 0101 1100</code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="box box-blue fragment">
                            <h4>2. Assembly Language</h4>
                            <p class="small-text">Uses <strong>Mnemonics</strong> (short codes) to represent machine
                                code.</p>
                            <pre><code class="assembly">LDA First
ADD Second
STO Sum</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- VERTICAL: Comparison -->
                <section>
                    <h3>Comparison</h3>
                    <div class="cols-3">
                        <div class="box">
                            <strong>High-Level</strong>
                            <ul class="small-text">
                                <li><i class="fa-solid fa-check green"></i> Easy to debug</li>
                                <li><i class="fa-solid fa-check green"></i> Portable</li>
                                <li><i class="fa-solid fa-xmark red"></i> Slower execution</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="box box-blue">
                            <strong>Low-Level</strong>
                            <ul class="small-text">
                                <li><i class="fa-solid fa-check green"></i> Fast execution</li>
                                <li><i class="fa-solid fa-check green"></i> Hardware control</li>
                                <li><i class="fa-solid fa-xmark red"></i> Hard to learn</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="box" style="background:#fff3cd; border-left-color:#ffc107;">
                            <strong>Why use Assembly?</strong>
                            <p class="small-text">To write device drivers or code that needs to run extremely fast (e.g.
                                games engines).</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Did You Know?</h3>
                <div class="cols">
                    <div class="box">
                        <h4><i class="fa-solid fa-microchip"></i> Different CPUs, Different Code</h4>
                        <p class="small-text fragment">Machine code depends on the CPU architecture (e.g., x86 vs ARM).</p>
                        <p class="small-text fragment">That’s why software often needs to be compiled for the right platform.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="box-blue">
                        <h4><i class="fa-solid fa-mobile-screen"></i> Phones Are ARM</h4>
                        <p class="small-text fragment">Most smartphones use ARM processors.</p>
                        <p class="small-text fragment">Apps are built/translated to run on that hardware.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 5. CONCEPT LOOP: Translators -->
            <section>
                <section>
                    <h2>Translators</h2>
                    <p>Software that converts code into machine code.</p>
                    <div class="cols-3">
                        <div class="fragment box">
                            <h4>Assembler</h4>
                            <p class="small-text">Assembly &rarr; Machine Code.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="fragment box box-blue">
                            <h4>Compiler</h4>
                            <p class="small-text">HLL &rarr; Machine Code (All at once).</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="fragment box box-blue">
                            <h4>Interpreter</h4>
                            <p class="small-text">HLL &rarr; Machine Code (Line by line).</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div style="margin-top: 20px; text-align: center;">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-down blue"></i> <span class="small-text blue">Deep Dive: Compiler vs
                            Interpreter</span>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- VERTICAL: Compiler vs Interpreter -->
                <section data-background="#f4f6f8">
                    <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group"></i> Deep Dive: Compiler vs Interpreter</h3>
                    <p class="small-text">Crucial for the exam!</p>
                    <div class="cols">
                        <div class="box box-blue">
                            <h4><i class="fa-solid fa-file-code"></i> Compiler</h4>
                            <ul class="small-text">
                                <li>Translates <strong>whole program</strong> at once.</li>
                                <li>Creates an <strong>Executable (.exe)</strong> file.</li>
                                <li>Reports errors <strong>at the end</strong>.</li>
                                <li><strong>Use:</strong> Distributing finished software.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="box">
                            <h4><i class="fa-solid fa-terminal"></i> Interpreter</h4>
                            <ul class="small-text">
                                <li>Translates <strong>one line at a time</strong>.</li>
                                <li>Does <strong>NOT</strong> create an executable.</li>
                                <li>Stops at the <strong>first error</strong>.</li>
                                <li><strong>Use:</strong> Developing/Testing code.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- HORIZONTAL: Scenario Check -->
                <section data-background="#003366">
                    <h3 style="color:white">Scenario Check</h3>
                    <p style="color:white; font-size:0.8em;">You want to sell a video game you made. You don't want
                        people to see or steal your source code. Which translator do you use?</p>
                    <div class="fragment answer-fragment"
                        style="background:white; color:#333; padding:15px; border-radius:5px;">
                        <strong>Compiler</strong>
                        <p class="small-text">It creates a standalone .exe file. The user doesn't need the source code
                            or the translator installed.</p>
                    </div>
                </section>
            </section>

            <!-- 6. CONCEPT LOOP: IDEs -->
            <section>
                <section>
                    <h2>The IDE</h2>
                    <div class="box-blue fragment" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
                        <p style="margin:0;"><strong>IDE</strong> (Integrated Development Environment) provides tools to write, run, and debug code in one place.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="fragment fade-in">
                        <p class="small-text">Examples: PyCharm, Visual Studio, IDLE.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="margin-top: 20px; text-align: center;">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-down blue"></i> <span class="small-text blue">Deep Dive:
                            Features</span>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- VERTICAL: IDE Features -->
                <section data-background="#f4f6f8">
                    <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group"></i> Deep Dive: IDE Features</h3>
                    <div class="cols-3">
                        <div class="box fragment">
                            <strong>Code Editor</strong><br>
                            <span class="small-text">Writes text. Uses <strong>Prettyprinting</strong> (colour coding)
                                to make code readable.</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="box box-blue fragment">
                            <strong>Translator</strong><br>
                            <span class="small-text">Built-in Compiler or Interpreter to run code instantly.</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="box fragment">
                            <strong>Debugger</strong><br>
                            <span class="small-text">Finds logic errors. Uses <strong>Breakpoints</strong> and
                                <strong>Variable Watch</strong>.</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="box box-blue fragment">
                            <strong>Error Diagnostics</strong><br>
                            <span class="small-text">Highlights syntax errors as you type.</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="box fragment">
                            <strong>Auto-completion</strong><br>
                            <span class="small-text">Predicts commands to speed up typing.</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="box box-blue fragment">
                            <strong>Auto-correction</strong><br>
                            <span class="small-text">Suggests fixes for common mistakes.</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h3>Quick Check</h3>
                <div class="question-box">Which translator creates an <strong>executable</strong> file?</div>
                <div class="fragment box-blue" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Compiler</strong> — it translates the whole program into an executable.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h3>Quick Check</h3>
                <div class="question-box">Which IDE feature helps you find logic errors by stepping through code?</div>
                <div class="fragment box-blue" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Debugger</strong></p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 7. EXIT TICKET -->
            <section>
